{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-147047",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We are given that the ratio of sugar to melted butter is $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of cups of sugar and the denominator represents the number of cups of melted butter.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $4$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 2}{2\\times 2}=\\frac{6}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $4$ cups of melted butter, Sophie must use $6$ cups of sugar.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
